 ## First Action
 
 Run `git diff` to inspect the actual code changes. If the diff is large or ambiguous, read the changed files directly. Do not trust the implementer report as source of truth.
 
+## Shopify Binks Review
+
+This Shopify-host override attempts one best-effort local Binks review per task.
+Hosted PR Binks remains authoritative. Keep local run state only in the active session.
+
+1. Run `binks-review --check-repository-eligibility` in the repository before
+   dispatching. Continue only when it exits zero. The helper accepts only an
+   `origin` on the exact `github.com` host in the exact `Shopify` or `shop`
+   organization, case-insensitively.
+2. On any nonzero result, do not dispatch `binks-reviewer`. Record
+   `BINKS: SKIPPED_INELIGIBLE_REPOSITORY` and continue the normal Kiro review.
+3. For an eligible repository, look in the current session context for an
+   `## External Review Handoff` with `SOURCE: BINKS` for this exact task.
+4. Reuse an existing same-task handoff without dispatching another run. Record
+   `BINKS: REUSED`. The controller passes it into later reviewer rounds for the
+   same task.
+5. If no same-task handoff is present, the main/controller applying this
+   protocol dispatches one `binks-reviewer` with the repository path, task
+   context, boundary/spec refs, and intended PR base when known. This protocol
+   authorizes that one read-only run.
+6. In autonomous `kiro-impl`, the parent performs the eligibility check and
+   dispatch before spawning the task reviewer. Direct main-context use does the
+   same.
+7. If dispatch times out, errors, returns malformed output or no handoff, or the
+   handoff has `RUN_STATUS: UNAVAILABLE`, record `BINKS: UNAVAILABLE` with the
+   reason and continue the normal Kiro review without retrying. This MUST NOT
+   reject or block the task, require manual verification, or trigger debugging.
+8. A nested task reviewer consumes caller-supplied Binks state and must not
+   launch another nested reviewer. Missing state from an eligible parent is
+   `BINKS: UNAVAILABLE`, not a review rejection.
+9. Keep a returned handoff in session context only. Never write a marker,
+   cache, task annotation, or other durable run state. If context is lost, a
+   later review may dispatch another run.
+10. A reused handoff describes its recorded worktree fingerprint, not the
+    current worktree. Verify `VALID` or `NEEDS_CONTEXT` findings independently;
+    only a confirmed current finding can affect the Kiro verdict. False positives
+    and unconfirmed findings do not reject the task.
+11. Never send Binks availability failures to the implementer for remediation.
+
 ## Core Principle
 
 Read the spec yourself. Read the diff yourself. Verify mechanically where possible. Reject on concrete failures rather than interpretive optimism.
